    {
      "id": "cN5X_fhMN_dxXN45ni_bC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 31.67793084013738,
      "y": 763.4109568244272,
      "width": 1116.2023093729197,
      "height": 606.4295546296902,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4B",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1378060691,
      "version": 566,
      "versionNonce": 796574909,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792443247056,
      "created": 1792443229847,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TOP 3 RISKS & FIXES\n\n1. SQL Injection in Login (Flows 3/4, 11/12) | Risk 25\n   Issue: Credentials concatenated into the SQL query;\n          anyone can bypass login and access all data.\n   Fix:   Parameterized queries; generic error messages.\n\n2. OS Command Injection in Admin Ping (Flows 18/19) | Risk 20\n   Issue: Host input executed via a shell, as root;\n          arbitrary commands run on the server.\n   Fix:   Host allow-list; argument list, no shell;\n          non-root container; host mounts removed.\n\n3. Broken Access Control / IDOR (Flows 7/8, 15/16) | Risk 16\n   Issue: No ownership check; users can read or edit\n          other users' grades by changing the record ID.\n   Fix:   Server-side ownership checks on every\n          read/write (404 / 403 if not authorized).",
      "fontSize": 26.95242465020845,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TOP 3 RISKS & FIXES\n\n1. SQL Injection in Login (Flows 3/4, 11/12) | Risk 25\n   Issue: Credentials concatenated into the SQL query;\n          anyone can bypass login and access all data.\n   Fix:   Parameterized queries; generic error messages.\n\n2. OS Command Injection in Admin Ping (Flows 18/19) | Risk 20\n   Issue: Host input executed via a shell, as root;\n          arbitrary commands run on the server.\n   Fix:   Host allow-list; argument list, no shell;\n          non-root container; host mounts removed.\n\n3. Broken Access Control / IDOR (Flows 7/8, 15/16) | Risk 16\n   Issue: No ownership check; users can read or edit\n          other users' grades by changing the record ID.\n   Fix:   Server-side ownership checks on every\n          read/write (404 / 403 if not authorized).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
